<h1 class="my-4">Terms of Use for special collections materials</h1>

<p>These terms govern your access to and use of special collections materials held by Stanford University Libraries repositories, including Special Collections &amp; University Archives, the Archive of Recorded Sound, the David Rumsey Map Center, and East Asia Library. They apply to materials in both physical and digital formats.</p>

<h2 class="h3 my-4">Use of collections</h2>
<p>You will comply with the policies and instructions of the Stanford University Libraries reading room you visit.
  Access to materials is subject to availability and collection restrictions. Stanford University Libraries may limit or refuse service when necessary, including in cases of noncompliance or emergency.</p>

<h2 class="h3 my-4">Care and photography of materials</h2>
<p>You will handle all materials carefully and follow staff instructions for their use.</p>
<p>You will not mark, damage, alter, or misuse materials.</p>
<p>You may photograph materials yourself when permitted by the applicable reading room and collection policies. Photography practices, equipment allowances, and restrictions may vary. You must follow staff instructions.</p>

<h2 class="h3 my-4">Copyright and publication</h2>
<p>You are responsible for complying with copyright and other applicable laws when using, reproducing, publishing, or distributing materials.</p>
<p>You are responsible for determining the copyright status of the materials you use, assessing whether your intended use of materials requires rightsholder permission, and for obtaining any necessary permission from the rights holder.</p>
<p>You agree to indemnify Stanford University against claims arising from your publication or other use of materials from Stanford University Libraries.</p>

<h2 class="h3 my-4">Digitization services</h2>
<p>Stanford University Libraries staff can create digital reproductions of materials, including scans and photographs, upon request.</p>
<p>All requests are reviewed by reading room staff. Requests may be denied based on collection restrictions (such as embargoes), material condition, copyright restrictions, or technical feasibility. Service options, fees, and turnaround times vary by reading room and collection. Stanford University Libraries reserves the right to decline any digitization request.</p>

<h2 class="h3 my-4">Account information</h2>
<p>Stanford University Libraries may retain information collected in connection with your use of the Stanford University Libraries Special Collections Research Account indefinitely.</p>
<p>Information is stored by Atlas Systems, Inc., a third party vendor, and will not be shared unless required by law.</p>

